{"key":"enterprise/T1564.012","id":"T1564.012","name":"File/Path Exclusions","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1564","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may attempt to hide their file-based artifacts by writing them to specific folders or file names excluded from antivirus (AV) scanning and other defensive capabilities. AV and other file-based scanners often include exclusions to optimize performance as well as ease installation and legitimate use of applications. These exclusions may be contextual (e.g., scans are only initiated in response to specific triggering events/alerts), but…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1564/012","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--09b008a9-b4eb-462a-a751-a0eb58050cd9","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.620Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0051","name":"Detection Strategy for File/Path Exclusions","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0051","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--f91754